WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.500
What if Superman was in Game of&nbsp;
Thrones? It seems like fans are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:08.520
going to great lengths to make that&nbsp;
very thing happen–in a way, at least.

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:14.820
Henry Cavill is someone who is well aware of the&nbsp;
Game of Thrones and The Witcher comparisons that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:19.740
have been floating around the internet for years&nbsp;
now. And, thanks to the fan artist BossLogic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:25.620
we can actually see what the star looks like&nbsp;
as a descendant of Valyria, and it's epic.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.180
Back in December 2019, at the&nbsp;
height of the Targaryen talk&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.020
and ahead of the The Witcher Season&nbsp;
1, Henry told Entertainment Tonight:

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.420
"I think comparisons are always going to be made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:40.860
and it's fun. It's fine when they're two&nbsp;
ends of a spectrum in a fantasy genre."

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.900
Appearing on Jimmy Kimmel Live that same month,&nbsp;
Cavill jokingly told the late-night host,

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:50.220
"I modeled myself after Khaleesi.&nbsp;
I made people call me Khaleesi or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:53.880
Emilia on set. I want to be Emilia or Khaleesi."

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:55.982
"Call me mother of dragons. I'm fine."

00:00:55.982 --> 00:01:01.140
It's no secret that Henry is a huge fan of&nbsp;
fantasy and fiction — whether it be books,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:06.660
movies, television shows, comics, or video&nbsp;
games. BossLogic and other fan artists have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:11.220
imagined him in a number of different&nbsp;
franchises and famous forms, including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:17.340
Wolverine and James Bond. But seeing Cavill as&nbsp;
a Targaryen may truly be the most incredible.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:23.580
Hide your dragons, folks, because Henry Cavill is&nbsp;
officially here as a member of House Targaryen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:29.460
BossLogic shared the awesome fan casting in&nbsp;
late August, through his social media channels.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:32.280
On the post, the creator joked:

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.480
"The hair checks out."

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:39.060
This is in reference to Cavill's similar silver&nbsp;
hairstyle in The Witcher. BossLogic's image of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:43.800
Cavill was accompanied by a House of the Dragon&nbsp;
banner at the bottom, which debuted in August&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:50.280
2022 and seemingly inspired him. Franchise fans&nbsp;
and viewers have been eating the fan casting up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.480
with many calling for studio execs to&nbsp;
take notice. One Twitter user wrote:

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:59.220
"Henry Cavill would make a badass Aegon&nbsp;
the Conqueror. Or...Young Jaeharys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:02.100
Adult Aegon V, Baelor the Blessed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.100 --> 00:02:07.620
Aegon the Unworthy (in his early years).&nbsp;
JUST GIVE CAVILL A COOL TARGARYEN ROLE."

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:09.000
Someone else tweeted,

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:14.940
"What other man would we deem worthy to cast&nbsp;
as rider of Balerion The Black Dread? A dragon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.940 --> 00:02:20.340
so large it could swallow a fully armored&nbsp;
Knight on Horseback with one snatch of its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:26.460
Mighty Jaw. Wielding the mighty Valyrian Blade,&nbsp;
Blackfyre. I see no other choice. He's my Aegon."

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:31.560
That all said, what makes the Cavill fan&nbsp;
casting truly epic for Game of Thrones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:36.540
and House of the Dragon fans is the fact&nbsp;
that Cavill isn't just some George R.R.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:41.400
Martin novice. For those who aren't aware,&nbsp;
Henry Cavill is someone who is not only a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:46.620
fan of the Game of Thrones HBO series, but&nbsp;
also the books that inspired it. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.000
he's even managed to convince others in&nbsp;
Hollywood to read them and was able to pass&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:56.700
on his fandom to at least one of his previous&nbsp;
co-stars — Laurence Fishburne. Conleth Hill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:01.440
a Game of Thrones actor and family friend of&nbsp;
Laurence, explained in an interview with Vulture:

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:05.340
"He was about to watch the show, and&nbsp;
Henry Cavill was the one who told him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:10.620
'No, no, no, read the books first.’ So he&nbsp;
became a fan of A Song of Ice and Fire,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:15.780
all the Game of Thrones books. He's read them&nbsp;
all. And then [Fishburne's wife] showed me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:20.580
a text from Laurence that said, 'Welcome,&nbsp;
master of whisperers and your little birds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:24.120
too,' or something like that, which&nbsp;
was very sweet of both of them."

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:28.680
Back in April 2021, Cavill posted a&nbsp;
photo online that showed him playing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:32.820
a Game of Thrones chess set with his&nbsp;
girlfriend. A Twitter user responded,

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:35.280
"He shouldn't be playing on&nbsp;
a Game of Thrones chess set.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:37.680
He should have been playing on Game of Thrones."

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:43.680
With House of the Dragon already appearing to be&nbsp;
a major hit for HBO, it's not completely out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:48.928
the question for Cavill to appear on the show&nbsp;
one day as a Targaryen. Only time will tell.

